  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read http_profile.request_envelope and proxy.outstanding_id_provenance. The request envelope is untouched; in envelope/response.rs validate_response_envelope was split into require_jsonrpc_version, response_outcome, require_error_shape, require_response_only and require_correlation, and the checks run in the same order with the same refusal clauses (not an object, jsonrpc, both or neither of result and error, error shape, result not an object, method or params present, id absent or mismatched, a notification never correlating); the in-file tests are unchanged. On the serving side a search of mcp-re-proxy/src shows validate_request_envelope called once in production, in request_admission.rs, and the decided OutstandingId is carried by the admitted envelope to answer_dispatched, which now receives it together with the dispatched exchange rather than as a separate argument; every other call is inside a test module. outstanding_id_provenance_test.rs is unchanged. The claim, scope and premises are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor.",
